## Target and Role

**Target:** GitHub Copilot Agent Mode operating in the existing SentinelOps repository.

Act as a **Principal Software Architect, Senior Full-Stack Engineer, ASP.NET Core/PostgreSQL Engineer, Offline-First Synchronization Specialist, Application Security Engineer, and QA/Release Engineer**.

Your task is to remediate the findings in the **SentinelOps Application Audit dated 2026-10-29**. Work in the repository, make the necessary code and test changes, and verify the results. Do not merely restate the audit or provide a plan and stop.

## Mission and Project Context

SentinelOps is primarily an offline-first PWA using browser IndexedDB. A React/TypeScript frontend, an ASP.NET Core API, and PostgreSQL synchronization foundation already exist. The application supports local CRM, quotations/revisions, invoices, payments, projects, PDF generation, backups, local authentication, and an IndexedDB outbox.

The audit's concern is that the shared-cloud layer is not yet production-ready for real financial data. Do not treat the existence of an API or PostgreSQL models as proof of complete cloud persistence or multi-device synchronization. Preserve local-first operation while improving server authority, security, synchronization, recoverability, and operational verification.

The audit file is the current source of the findings and P0–P3 definitions. Locate and read the complete report in the repository before editing. Verify each finding against the latest code; do not assume audit paths or state remain unchanged.

